define phrase wires-from-base
  Looking straight up, you can see four support wires attached to the top of
  the center post, stretching in four directions.
end phrase

define phrase wires-out-of-reach
  The wires are too high up for you to reach, and you can't get to where they
  are attached on the ground.
end phrase

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## GRUBBER'S MARKET AS A THING (`story.ni:3548-3617`) — the market named:
## what it looks like from each place, what it smells and sounds like, and
## `enter market` from wherever she stands. The alley and tent arms walk
## her out (an authorial move behind the same guards the exits carry — the
## alley's voices, a holding mercenary, the chase's sealed tent); the roof,
## the top and the space behind the tent refuse; the market proper is
## "already". The entity is `enterable` MECHANICALLY: a clause's `move`
## statements ride postExecute, which only a successful enter reaches, and
## the refusal ladder covers every room but the two walk-outs — so the
## trait is never player-visible except as the source's own behaviour. The
## walk narrates no destination (the ADR-326 D5 seam); `look` answers.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

create Grubber's Market
  aka market, grubbers, grubbers market, grubber, square, market square, outer ring, center, centre, market center, aisle, aisles, hub, central hub, main market, bustle, bustling market
  scenery, enterable, proper
  in the Northwest Junction

  The market is bustling this morning.

  when Jack moves, while within-grubbers
    move Grubber's Market here
  end when

  on the player examining
    phrase market-from-alley when the player is in the Alley
    phrase market-from-roof when the player is in the Outer Market Roof
    phrase market-from-tent when the player is in Inside the Silk Tent
    phrase market-from-back when the player is in the Base of the Center Post
    phrase market-from-top when the player is in the Top of the Post
  end on

  on the player smelling
    phrase market-smell
  end on

  on the player listening
    phrase market-sound
  end on

  on the player entering
    refuse when the player is in the Outer Market Roof or the player is in the Top of the Post: market-get-down
    refuse when the player is in the Base of the Center Post: market-behind-tent
    refuse when open-air: market-already-here
    refuse when the player is in the Alley and the voices is here: alley-stay-hidden
    refuse when the wandering mercenaries is here and the wandering mercenaries is aggressive: merc-held
    refuse when the player is in Inside the Silk Tent and chase: tent-no-way-back
    move the player to the Northwest Junction when the player is in the Alley
    move the player to Outside the Silk Tent when the player is in Inside the Silk Tent
  end on

define phrase market-from-alley
  You can't see the market from back here in the alley.
end phrase

define phrase market-from-roof
  You can see the northwest corner of the market from up here.
end phrase

define phrase market-from-tent
  You can't see the market from inside Teisha's tent.
end phrase

define phrase market-from-back
  You can't see much of the market from back here behind the stalls.
end phrase

define phrase market-from-top
  The market spreads out beneath you in all directions.
end phrase

define phrase market-smell
  The market smells of a mixture of all sorts of odors: dust and sweat, leather
  and sawdust, spices, fruits, and groceries.
end phrase

define phrase market-sound
  The market is a cacophony of sounds, with dozens of merchants hawking their
  wares and scores of shoppers haggling over the price.
end phrase

define phrase market-get-down
  You'll have to get down first.
end phrase

define phrase market-behind-tent
  You'll have to get out from behind Teisha's tent first.
end phrase

define phrase market-already-here
  You're already in the market.
end phrase

## Kept aside — the source's `departing` lines (`story.ni:3610-3616`),
## unreachable in 2009 (no grammar defines the action) and so not carried:
##   "There's only two ways out of Grubber's: north from Northwest Junction,
##   or east from East Junction."

