## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## A BARE `smell` AND `listen` — the source's per-room answers, in the order
## Inform resolved them: a room's own `Instead` first, then the market
## backdrop's line wherever the backdrop stands, then the report rulebook's
## fallback. Every line in a body fires when its guard holds, so the guards
## partition the rooms.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

define action sniffing
  grammar
    smell
    sniff

  phrase garbage-ripe-here when the player is in the Alley
  phrase leather-smell when the player is in the Leather Stall
  phrase tallow-fumes-smell when the player is in the Candle Stall
  phrase fruit-stall-smell when the player is in the Fruit Stall
  phrase tent-smell when the player is in Inside the Silk Tent
  phrase top-of-post-smell when the player is in the Top of the Post
  phrase market-smell when market-air
  phrase smell-nothing when not within-grubbers

define action hearkening
  grammar
    listen
    hear

  phrase alley-strain-to-hear when the player is in the Alley and the voices is here
  phrase market-sound when the player is in the Alley and the voices is not here
  phrase roof-listen-carefully when the player is in the Outer Market Roof and the group of mercenaries is here
  phrase market-sound when the player is in the Outer Market Roof and the group of mercenaries is not here
  phrase tent-sound when the player is in Inside the Silk Tent
  phrase top-of-post-sound when the player is in the Top of the Post
  phrase market-sound when market-din
  phrase ears-pricked when not within-grubbers

define phrase garbage-ripe-here
  It smells pretty ripe back here.
end phrase

define phrase fruit-stall-smell
  It smells delicious here.
end phrase

define phrase tent-smell
  It smells of warm, dusty fabric in here.
end phrase

define phrase tent-sound
  The sounds of the market are muffled in here.
end phrase

define phrase top-of-post-smell
  The air is fresh up here, although the scents of the market drift up faintly
  from below.
end phrase

define phrase top-of-post-sound
  It is relatively quiet and peaceful up here, although the sounds of the
  market drift up faintly from below.
end phrase

define phrase smell-nothing
  You smell nothing unexpected.
end phrase

define phrase ears-pricked
  You keep your ears pricked.
end phrase
